# .assay-surfaces — declared risk-surface globs for the mechanical verdict-time surface tier.
#
# CONTRACT
#   - One glob per line. Blank lines and lines whose first non-space character is '#' are
#     ignored. A path may contain '#', so an inline trailing comment is NOT stripped — put a
#     comment on its own line.
#   - A PR is labelled `surface:core` when ANY changed path matches ANY glob here, and
#     `surface:std` otherwise. A repo with NO .assay-surfaces file is labelled with neither
#     (three-state: "no declared surfaces" is never guessed as std).
#   - The label is ADVISORY — a merge-queue triage aid for the single human merge gate. It
#     GATES NOTHING. (The fail-closed security gate is a separate, compiled+env mechanism;
#     this file is not that.)
#
# GLOB SYNTAX (a small, gitignore-flavoured subset — see deskkit.MatchSurfaceGlob)
#   *   matches any run of characters within one path segment (e.g. *guard* matches
#       "writeguard"); it never crosses a '/'.
#   **  as a whole path segment matches zero or more segments (e.g. dir/** matches
#       everything under dir/, at any depth, and **/x matches x at any depth).
#
# The globs below name THIS repository's real risk surfaces: CI workflow definitions, the
# advisory guardrails doc, the guard command tools, and the git hooks. (An adopter repo
# supplies its own surfaces; the labeler reads whatever this file declares and never bakes
# any one repo's layout into the tool.)

.github/workflows/**
.claude/guardrails/**
tools/desk/cmd/*guard*/**
tools/desk/hooks/**
